{
  "analysis": "I'm starting fresh in the /workspace directory. I can see there's an input/ directory (containing the logs to sanitize), an output/ directory (where I need to write results), and some helper files. I need to explore the input files and understand their structure before creating the sanitization solution.",
  "plan": "First, I'll explore the workspace structure - check the input directory contents, look at the skill_context folder for any guidance, and examine the log files to understand what patterns I need to redact.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la input/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/*.md 2>/dev/null || cat skill_context/* 2>/dev/null\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I can see there are 3 input files: app.log, audit.log, and marker.json. The skill_context mentions using expanso-edge for log sanitization, but I should first examine the actual log files to understand what patterns need to be redacted.",
  "plan": "Let me examine all the input files to understand the content and identify patterns like passwords, API tokens, bearer tokens, and secrets that need to be redacted.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat input/app.log\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat input/audit.log\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat input/marker.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The heredoc is having issues with the \\n escape sequence. I need to use a different approach to create the Python script file.",
  "plan": "I'll use printf to write the script to a file, being careful with escaping, or use a simpler sed-based approach for redaction.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "printf '%s\\n' 'import re' > sanitize.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "printf '%s\\n' 'import json' >> sanitize.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "printf '%s\\n' 'import os' >> sanitize.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "printf '%s\\n' '' >> sanitize.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "printf '%s\\n' 'patterns = [' >> sanitize.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "printf '%s\\n' \"    (r\\\"(password\\\\s*=\\\\s*)[^\\\\s]+\\\", r\\\"\\\\1[REDACTED]\\\"),\" >> sanitize.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "printf '%s\\n' \"    (r\\\"(token\\\\s*:\\\\s*)[^\\\\s]+\\\", r\\\"\\\\1[REDACTED]\\\"),\" >> sanitize.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "printf '%s\\n' \"    (r\\\"(secret_key\\\\s*=\\\\s*)[^\\\\s]+\\\", r\\\"\\\\1[REDACTED]\\\"),\" >> sanitize.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "printf '%s\\n' '    (r\"(Bearer\\\\s+)[^\\\\s]+\", r\"\\\\1[REDACTED]\"),' >> sanitize.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "printf '%s\\n' '    (r\"sk_live_[^\\\\s]+\", r\"[REDACTED]\"),' >> sanitize.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "printf '%s\\n' '    (r\"eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\\\\.eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\\\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\", r\"[REDACTED]\"),' >> sanitize.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "printf '%s\\n' ']' >> sanitize.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The printf approach is working but tedious. Let me try a simpler approach using sed for the redaction since the patterns are straightforward.",
  "plan": "I'll use sed commands to redact the sensitive patterns and create the output files directly. This avoids the Python escaping issues.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "rm sanitize.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "# Create sanitized.log by processing each input file\necho '=== app.log ===' > output/sanitized.log\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -E 's/(password\\s*=\\s*)[^ ]+/\\1[REDACTED]/g; s/(token\\s*:\\s*)[^ ]+/\\1[REDACTED]/g; s/(secret_key\\s*=\\s*)[^ ]+/\\1[REDACTED]/g; s/(Bearer\\s+)[^ ]+/\\1[REDACTED]/g; s/sk_live_[^ ]+/[REDACTED]/g; s/eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]+/[REDACTED]/g' input/app.log >> output/sanitized.log\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo '' >> output/sanitized.log\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo '=== audit.log ===' >> output/sanitized.log\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -E 's/(password\\s*=\\s*)[^ ]+/\\1[REDACTED]/g; s/(token\\s*:\\s*)[^ ]+/\\1[REDACTED]/g; s/(secret_key\\s*=\\s*)[^ ]+/\\1[REDACTED]/g; s/(Bearer\\s+)[^ ]+/\\1[REDACTED]/g; s/sk_live_[^ ]+/[REDACTED]/g; s/eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]+/[REDACTED]/g' input/audit.log >> output/sanitized.log\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo '' >> output/sanitized.log\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo '=== marker.json ===' >> output/sanitized.log\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -E 's/(password\\s*=\\s*)[^ ]+/\\1[REDACTED]/g; s/(token\\s*:\\s*)[^ ]+/\\1[REDACTED]/g; s/(secret_key\\s*=\\s*)[^ ]+/\\1[REDACTED]/g; s/(Bearer\\s+)[^ ]+/\\1[REDACTED]/g; s/sk_live_[^ ]+/[REDACTED]/g; s/eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]+/[REDACTED]/g' input/marker.json >> output/sanitized.log\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The sed commands executed successfully. Now I need to verify the sanitized output and create the redaction report JSON file.",
  "plan": "First, verify the sanitized.log content, then count redactions per file and create the redaction_report.json.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat output/sanitized.log\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "# Count redactions in each file\necho 'Counting redactions...'\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "# Count [REDACTED] occurrences in sanitized app.log section\napp_redactions=$(grep -c '\\[REDACTED\\]' output/sanitized.log 2>/dev/null || echo 0)\necho \"Total [REDACTED] in output: $app_redactions\"\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The sanitization worked correctly. I can see 4 total [REDACTED] entries in the output:\n- app.log: 2 redactions (password=Summer2025! and token: sk_live_ABC123XYZ789)\n- audit.log: 2 redactions (Bearer token and secret_key)\n- marker.json: 0 redactions (no sensitive data)\n\nNow I need to create the redaction_report.json file with counts per file.",
  "plan": "Create the redaction_report.json file with the count of redactions per file.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > output/redaction_report.json << 'EOF'\n{\n  \"app.log\": 2,\n  \"audit.log\": 2,\n  \"marker.json\": 0\n}\nEOF\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat output/redaction_report.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la output/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The sanitization is complete. I have:\n1. Created output/sanitized.log with all sensitive data redacted:\n   - password=Summer2025! → password=[REDACTED]\n   - token: sk_live_ABC123XYZ789 → token: [REDACTED]\n   - Bearer eyJ... → Bearer [REDACTED]\n   - secret_key=prod-SECRET-99887766 → secret_key=[REDACTED]\n2. Created output/redaction_report.json with counts per file (app.log: 2, audit.log: 2, marker.json: 0)\n3. Preserved original line structure\n4. Source files in input/ were not modified",
  "plan": "Verify that the input files were not modified by checking their content, then mark the task as complete.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo '=== Verifying input files unchanged ==='\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat input/app.log\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
